     "Robert Mugabe led Zimbabwe from independence in 1980 until a military takeover forced him out in November 2017; he died in 2019. A former teacher and guerrilla leader, he was first praised abroad for reconciliation and for expanding schools and clinics. From the late 1990s, facing a strong opposition, he leaned on war veterans and land seizures to keep power. He blamed the economic collapse on Western sanctions and saboteurs, and his government responded to inflation with price controls and arrests of shopkeepers rather than with budget cuts. The hyperinflation of 2007-08 happened under him and largely because of his government's choices.",
