     "Crowds walking across a concrete bridge over a narrow river, carrying suitcases and children.",
     "The Simon Bolivar International Bridge joins San Antonio del Tachira in Venezuela to Cucuta in Colombia. At the height of the crisis tens of thousands of people crossed it on some days: to buy food and medicine in Colombia and walk back, or to leave for good. Many walked on to Bogota, Quito, Lima and Santiago, a journey of weeks. By November 2024 about **7.9 million** Venezuelans lived abroad, with more than 6.7 million in Latin America and the Caribbean. Their remittances became one of the main sources of dollars for the families left behind, helping to dollarise the economy from below.",
     "Hyperinflation's largest human consequence was migration on a scale few countries outside war have seen.",
